    "question": "接上太阳能板就不工作 The Gate Opener Quits Working Once Solar Panels Connected",
    "heading_level": 2,
    "answer_zh": "检查太阳能板（开路测试）\n断开太阳能板与TCS3之间的连接，断开各块太阳能板之间的连接，在无遮挡的正午阳光下，测量每一块太阳能板的开路电压\n正常值：>42VDC\n如果某块板明显低于42VDC → 该太阳能板损坏\n检查电池电压\n断开TCS3与电池之间的连接, 测量电池电压\n如果电压 <22VDC → 用外部充电器将电池充到24VDC以上，再重新接入系统\n测试TCS3是否正常（断开太阳能板）\n保持太阳能板断开, 仅连接电池到TCS3, 测量以下端口：\n端口正常值\t                   异常判断\nBAT端口\t= 电池电压; 若异常 → TCS3可能内部BAT通路故障\nLOAD端口>22VDC\t; 若低于22VDC或为0 → TCS3损坏\n如果BAT和LOAD均正常 → TCS3是好的，继续第4步\n接回太阳能板，整体验证\n接回太阳能板到TCS3, 测量以下端口，三者应大致等于电池电压\nSOL端口≈ 电池电压\nBAT端口\t≈ 电池电压\nLOAD端口≈ 电池电压\n如果端口电压异常→ 太阳能板损坏\n电池耗电异常 Abnormal Battery Drain\n确认电池规格、接线正确（一般需24V 12Ah或2×12V 12Ah串联），\n纯太阳能且无市电时：每增加一个持续耗电配件（如对射/有线键盘/外接收器等）建议太阳能板增加约30W；若有效阳光不足6小时/天或门机每天开关超过10次，也需加大太阳能板和电池容量。\n断开其他额外用电设备（如是否给其他外部用电器供电，如：备用灯、门禁读卡器等）。\n拔掉所有配件及机臂，看是否还异常耗电。\n还不行的话，换一组新的符合规格的电池试试。\n好了 → 电池问题。\n没好 → 继续下一步。\n断开TCS3与控制板的连接。（用TCS3）\n依然耗电 → TCS3问题。\n不耗电了 → 接回空控制板（不接配件）。\n又耗电 → 控制板问题。\n不耗电 → 机臂或某个配件问题（逐个接回排查）。",
    "answer_en": "Check the solar panel(s) – open circuit voltage test\nDisconnect all solar panels from the TCS3 and also disconnect the panels from each other. Under direct sunlight with no shading, preferably around noon, measure the open circuit voltage of each solar panel. A normal reading should be above 42 VDC. If any panel shows a voltage significantly lower than 42 VDC, that solar panel is faulty and should be replaced.\nCheck the battery voltage\nDisconnect the battery from the TCS3 and measure battery voltage.\nIf the battery voltage is above 24 VDC, please proceed step 3.\nIf the voltage is below 22 VDC, use an external charger to charge the battery to above 24 VDC, then reconnect it to the TCS3 and continue test 3. If battery voltage is always below 22VDC even if fully charged, the batteries are defective and needs to be replaced.\nTest the TCS3 with solar panels disconnected\nKeep all solar panels disconnected and connect only the battery to the TCS3. Measure the voltage of BAT terminal and the LOAD terminal of the TCS3. The BAT terminal should read the approximately same as the battery voltage and the LOAD terminal should read above 22 VDC.\nIf the LOAD terminal voltage is below 22 VDC, the TCS3 is faulty.\nIf the BAT terminal voltage is below 22 VDC, replace the battery to have a try. If the problem remains, the TCS3 should be defective.\nIf both BAT and LOAD terminals show normal values, the TCS3 is good and you can proceed to Step 4.\nFinal test with solar panels connected\nReconnect the solar panels to the TCS3. Then measure the SOL terminal, BAT terminal, and LOAD terminal. Under normal operation, all three terminals should read approximately the same as the battery voltage. If any of these terminals shows an abnormal voltage, the solar panel should be faulty.\nPlease verify that the battery meet the required standards.\nGenerally, a 24V 12Ah battery (or 2pcs 12V 12Ah batteries connected in series may function as 24V) is required to power the gate opener. Lead acid / GEL / AGM / flooded (deep cycle) batteries can be used. Kindly note that the regulator is not compatible with most lithium-ion batteries, except for LiFePO4 batteries. And the battery should be waterproof type, or be placed in waterproof circumstance.\nMoreover, if you only use solar panels to charge the batteries (no AC electricity), you’re required to increase the solar panels power and the batteries capacity in the following situations:\nAdd continuously electricity-consuming accessories such as exit sensor wand, wired keypad, external receiver, etc. Normally, if you add such an accessory, you need to add 30W more solar panels.\nThere is less than 6 hours sunlight or the gate opener should be operated more than 10 cycles per day.\nThen check that all wiring is correct, especially the positive and negative connections and ensure  no loose or short-circuited connections are present.\nIf all above are verified, please disconnect any additional devices that may be powered by the same battery (e.g., auxiliary lights, access control readers, etc.).\nIf the battery is powering only the gate opener system, proceed to the next step.\nDisconnect all wired accessories and arms from the control board and leave only the main power input connected to the control board. If the problem persists, please move to step 4.\nTry another set of new batteries to have a try.\nIf the issue is resolved → The original battery is likely defective or has poor performance.\nIf the issue persists → Proceed to Step 5.\nDisconnect the TCS3 module from the control board. Leave the TCS3 connected only to the battery.\nIf abnormal drain continues → The TCS3 module is likely faulty and requires replacement.\nIf the drain stops → Proceed to Step 6.\nReconnect the TCS3 module to the control board. Ensure that no accessories and arms are connected to the control board (power only).\nIf the drain returns → The control board itself is likely faulty.\nIf there is no drain → The issue is caused by the arm or accessories. Reconnect arms and each accessory one by one to identify the faulty device.",
