    "question": "按遥控器保险丝烧 Fuse Blows When Pressing Remote",
    "heading_level": 2,
    "answer_zh": "1 检查端口接的线与线之间是否有铜丝触碰到，确认保险丝规格正确（∅5×20mm 10A 250VAC快断玻璃管）；\n2 断开控制板端口上的有线配件，机臂线，只保留电源接线，然后按遥控器；\n如果保险丝烧，检查控制板的输入电压，正常电压24VDC左右；如果电压没问题，那就是控制板坏，可以看看控制板表面是否有元器件短路痕迹；\n(2) 如果保险丝不烧，把机臂从门上拿下来，机臂电机线接回控制板，打开离合，按遥控器看看烧不烧，此时如果烧，问题在电机电流大，如果不烧，合上离合再按遥控器，如果烧，问题在机臂内部卡顿，手动推拉机臂是否顺畅；\n3如果没问题，把机臂装门上再按遥控器试试，如果这个时候烧 说明负载过大，可能门本身较重或卡顿，需要检查门本身是否可以推拉顺畅（可在距门铰链约1米/3.3英尺处手动开合测试），并问问门宽门重；\n4如果以上都好的，依次把有线配件接回去，逐一排查哪个配件导致烧控制板的。",
    "answer_en": "1 Verify no exposed copper strands are causing contact between wires at terminals. Confirm the fuse rating is correct (∅5*20mm 10A 250VAC fast blow glass fuse).\n2 Disconnect all wired accessories and the gate arms from the control board, leaving only the power supply connected. Press the remote to test.\nIf the fuse blows, measure the input voltage to the control board. The normal voltage should be around 24VDC. If the voltage is correct, the control board is likely faulty. Inspect the board surface for any signs of component short circuits. If the voltage is incorrect, check the power supply.\nIf the fuse does not blow: Remove the arms from the gate and reconnect one arm to the control board. Disengage the clutch and press the remote.\nIf the fuse blows, the motor is drawing excessive current.\nIf it does not blow, re-engage the clutch and press the remote again.\nIf it now blows, the internal mechanism of the arm is jammed. Check if the arm moves smoothly manually.\nIf does not blow, reconnect the other arm to the control board, disengage the clutch and press the remote to see if the other arm is normal.\n3 If the arm tests fine off the gate, reinstall one arm on the gate, operate it via remote.\nIf the fuse blows now, this indicates excessive load, likely due to a heavy or obstructed gate. Use the release key to disengage the clutch of the arm, and check whether the gate itself can be manually opened & closed freely 3.3 feet (one meter) away from the gate hinge. If not, please let me know the weight and length of your gate and double check the gate to make sure the gate can run freely by hand.\nIf the fuse doesn’t blow, please reinstall the other arm on the gate and press the remote to check how it works.\n4 If there is no problem after above steps, the problem lies in the wired accessories. Reconnect the accessories one at a time to identify the specific cause.",
